WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:04.434
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:05.701
This is it. You're here.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:09.167
Thank you for watching.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.367
Well, guys, this is exciting.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:13.701
The 2022 NFL season
kicked off tonight!

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:15.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.033
Right now, our viewers are like,

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.934
"Am I really drunk
or does Fallon have a beard?"

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:26.200
Oh, it was great to have
football on TV again.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.133
I haven't seen that
many slow-motion replays

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.234
since Harry Styles
sat next to Chris Pine.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.734
Do you know what I'm saying?
I really...

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:37.067
Yeah, tonight's game was between

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:39.567
the Buffalo Bills
and the Los Angeles Rams.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.434
Yep, Buffalo versus L.A.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.901
It was basically the wings
on your plate versus the celery.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.734
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.067
I saw that the Buffalo Bills

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:49.701
have the best odds
to win the Super Bowl.

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:52.267
Yeah. Meanwhile,
the team with the worst odds are

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:54.567
the Houston Texans.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:56.234
Yeah, they're not
supposed to be very good.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.234
Check out the billboards
they're using to sell tickets.

00:00:58.234 --> 00:00:59.234
This one says...

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.200
You see what I'm saying?

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.300
-That's the ad for the team.
-Yeah, this next one says...

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:14.701
I mean, that's cool.
I love Patrick Mahomes.

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:15.767
Finally, it says...

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:22.033
-Oh!
-Now, that's -- I would do it.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.701
I'd do it.
♪♪

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.634
But, you guys, everyone's
excited that the NFL is back,

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:29.968
and there's no better way
to celebrate

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.801
than with some
football banner fails.

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:32.801
Hit it!

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.300
♪♪

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:52.334
You can't beat it.

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:57.000
Well, every year, guys,
the NFL introduces new rules

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.801
that they're going to enforce
in the upcoming season.

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:01.667
And we actually got our hands on
some of the updated penalties,

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:03.100
and there's some
pretty interesting ones.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.033
Here, take a look.
This first penalty is for...

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.267
This next one is for...

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.334
And, finally,
there's a penalty for...

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:27.434
It's like, "'Dragon'?
"Lord of the..."

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:28.934
Speaking of,
did you guys see this?

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.501
In the most recent episode of
"House of the Dragon,"

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:35.534
fans noticed that HBO forgot to
cut out the green-screen glove

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:38.901
on a character who is supposed
to be missing two fingers.

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:41.801
Check this out. Look at this.
See if you can see. See it?

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:42.934
Yeah.

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:44.100
-Whoa!
-Yeah.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.367
People are upset.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.033
They want their show about
children riding dragons

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:53.133
to be 100% realistic.

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.400
Meanwhile, the CGI guy is like,

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.334
"Yeah, sorry about
those two teeny fingers.

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:57.667
I've been pretty busy, you know,

00:02:57.667 --> 00:03:01.367
with the dragons
fighting each other!

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:04.000
I haven't seen
my kids in years."

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.901
Worried about the fingers?

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:08.467
I got a finger for you."

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.834
No. Hey, hey.
Watch -- hey.

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.367
-Hey!
-Watch it.

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:15.200
-One of the Finger Lakes.
-Guys, get this.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.100
Today, former
Trump adviser Steve Bannon

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.234
turned himself in to
New York authorities

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:20.901
over an alleged
border-wall scheme

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:25.501
and was charged with conspiracy,
fraud, and money laundering.

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:26.968
Yeah. Can we see
Steve Bannon again?

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:29.367
I'll be honest.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:30.734
Based on that photo,
I don't think he's ever

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:31.767
laundered anything.

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:34.234
-Hey! Hey!

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:38.667
-When the judge asked Bannon how
he pleads, he said, "Grimy."

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.601
Yeah, Steve looked unkempt,
as usual.

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:42.234
The judge was like,
"Please approach the bench.

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.400
Eh, that's close enough."

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.300
Hey, guys, I read that the FDA
just approved

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.367
the new anti-wrinkle treatment
called Daxxify

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:52.100
that could be
Botox's biggest competitor.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.834
Yeah, right now,
the C.E.O. of Botox

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:56.534
is trying so hard to frown.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:07.467
If you're keeping track, there's
Botox, Daxxify,

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:10.534
and a third one that doesn't
work from Johnson &amp; Johnson.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:17.033
Guys, I heard
that Merriam-Webster

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:20.767
just added 370 new words
and terms to the dictionary,

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:24.634
including "sus," "yeet,"
and "metaverse."

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.300
Yeah, it's a move that the
Oxford dictionary

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.934
defines as "desperate."

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:31.133
Yeah.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:33.701
Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.334
Thank you all for watching.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:36.968
We got some sad news today.

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:39.000
We learned that
Queen Elizabeth II

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.167
passed away at the age of 96.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:44.300
And as a talk-show host, you
often get asked the question,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.834
"Who would be your dream guest?"

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:47.767
And my answer
was always the queen.

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:49.367
I've always been a fan.

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:51.601
I've admired the way
she conducted herself

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:54.300
always with
class, grace, and dignity.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.400
But, also,
she had a great sense of humor.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.033
She was very funny,
and I loved that about her.

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:01.000
She leaves behind
a great legacy,

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.968
and she'll be missed
but not forgotten.

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:04.834
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:05.968
Come on, back.

